{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"b390d3b57f5337ce","name":"card_unit_108_panzergrenadier","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/Germany/NavalWarfare/units/card_unit_108_panzergrenadier","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"108. PANZERGRENADIER","text":"Deployment: Convert target enemy unit with cost 4 or less into ROUTED TROOPS, then Retreat it.","flavorText":"The 108th Panzergrenadier Regiment was a unit of the 14th Panzer Division during WWII. The 14th Panzer Division was formed in 1940 from elements of the 4th Infantry Division and the 4th Panzer Division, and combined infantry and armored units. The 108th Panzergrenadier Regiment, alongside the 103rd, provided the division's mechanized infantry strength. In April 1941, the division participated in the invasion of Yugoslavia where it advanced swiftly to Sarajevo. Soon after it returned to Germany to prepare for Operation Barbarossa, and as part of Army Group South, it took part in the invasion of the Soviet Union in June 1941. The division engaged in continuous combat throughout the year and during the harsh winter on the Eastern Front. In early 1942, the division advanced through the Kharkov and Don regions as part of the German summer offensives. Later that year, the 14th Panzer Division was transferred to the 6th Army, which became encircled at Stalingrad. By February 1943, the division was destroyed in the battle. It was later reformed in Brittany, France, and by November 1943, it returned to the Eastern Front. The division continued to fight in various engagements until it became trapped in the Courland Pocket in early 1945, where it remained until Germany's surrender in May 1945.","faction":"Germany","type":"infantry","rarity":"Uncommon","cost":7,"operationCost":1,"attack":5,"defense":6},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_unit_108_panzergrenadier","title":{"Namespace":"card_germany","Key":"card_unit_108_panzergrenadier_title","SourceString":"108. PANZERGRENADIER","LocalizedString":"108. PANZERGRENADIER"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::infantry","attack":5,"defense":6,"range":1,"faction":"EFactionEnum::Germany","kredits":7,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_germany","Key":"card_unit_108_panzergrenadier_text","SourceString":"Deployment: Convert target enemy unit with cost 4 or less into ROUTED TROOPS, then Retreat it.","LocalizedString":"Deployment: Convert target enemy unit with cost 4 or less into ROUTED TROOPS, then Retreat it."},"flavorText":{"Namespace":"card_germany","Key":"card_unit_108_panzergrenadier_history","SourceString":"The 108th Panzergrenadier Regiment was a unit of the 14th Panzer Division during WWII. The 14th Panzer Division was formed in 1940 from elements of the 4th Infantry Division and the 4th Panzer Division, and combined infantry and armored units. The 108th Panzergrenadier Regiment, alongside the 103rd, provided the division's mechanized infantry strength. In April 1941, the division participated in the invasion of Yugoslavia where it advanced swiftly to Sarajevo. Soon after it returned to Germany to prepare for Operation Barbarossa, and as part of Army Group South, it took part in the invasion of the Soviet Union in June 1941. The division engaged in continuous combat throughout the year and during the harsh winter on the Eastern Front. In early 1942, the division advanced through the Kharkov and Don regions as part of the German summer offensives. Later that year, the 14th Panzer Division was transferred to the 6th Army, which became encircled at Stalingrad. By February 1943, the division was destroyed in the battle. It was later reformed in Brittany, France, and by November 1943, it returned to the Eastern Front. The division continued to fight in various engagements until it became trapped in the Courland Pocket in early 1945, where it remained until Germany's surrender in May 1945.","LocalizedString":"The 108th Panzergrenadier Regiment was a unit of the 14th Panzer Division during WWII. The 14th Panzer Division was formed in 1940 from elements of the 4th Infantry Division and the 4th Panzer Division, and combined infantry and armored units. The 108th Panzergrenadier Regiment, alongside the 103rd, provided the division's mechanized infantry strength. In April 1941, the division participated in the invasion of Yugoslavia where it advanced swiftly to Sarajevo. Soon after it returned to Germany to prepare for Operation Barbarossa, and as part of Army Group South, it took part in the invasion of the Soviet Union in June 1941. The division engaged in continuous combat throughout the year and during the harsh winter on the Eastern Front. In early 1942, the division advanced through the Kharkov and Don regions as part of the German summer offensives. Later that year, the 14th Panzer Division was transferred to the 6th Army, which became encircled at Stalingrad. By February 1943, the division was destroyed in the battle. It was later reformed in Brittany, France, and by November 1943, it returned to the Eastern Front. The division continued to fight in various engagements until it became trapped in the Courland Pocket in early 1945, where it remained until Germany's surrender in May 1945."},"operationCost":1,"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Uncommon","selectTargetOnPlayedFromHand":true,"cardSet":"ECardSetEnum::NavalWarfare","extraHelpTextBubbleTypes":["EHelpBubbleTypes::Retreat","EHelpBubbleTypes::Convert"],"draftBaseWeight":0.8,"hasDeployment":true,"spawnCardName":"card_unit_routed_troops","Image":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/Images/Germany/NavalWarfare/t_121_inantry_regiment.t_121_inantry_regiment","SubPathString":""},"artist":"David Pentland","historyPhoto":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/HistoricalPhotos/108__PANZERGRENADIER.108__PANZERGRENADIER","SubPathString":""},"historyPhotoSize":{"X":512.0,"Y":314.0},"historyPhotoDescription":{"Namespace":"card_germany","Key":"card_unit_108_panzergrenadier_photo","SourceString":"A Panzer III of the 14th Panzer Division and its crew on the East